      "content": "thanks for this. it's definitely heading in the right direction.\n\nmy only concern is the part where we mention the \"notable spike in Engineering.\" even if we attribute it to restructuring, the word \"spike\" itself is a bit of a magnet for questions. when the Board sees that word, their first instinct is going to be to ask for the actual number to see just how \"notable\" it is.\n\nat this level of reporting, we really want to avoid anything that creates a sense of volatility. is there a way we can refine this to be even more seamless? i'd like to move away from highlighting any specific departmental exceptions. can we focus the narrative entirely on the collective strength and the broader company-wide stability so we don't invite that kind of granular scrutiny?",
